{"qas": [
  {"question": "According to the EU AI Act as described in arXiv 2602.11944, what is the definition of 'risk' and how does it relate to high-risk AI systems?", "answer": "Risk is defined as the combination of the probability of an occurrence of harm and the severity of that harm. For high-risk AI systems, the goal is to bring this risk down to an acceptable level.", "evidence": [{"page": 19, "quote": "Risk\", in the understanding of the AI Act, is \"the combination of the probability of an occurrence of harm and the severity of that harm\" (Art. 3(2) AIA)."}, {"page": 19, "quote": "Where AI systems come with a high risk, the goal is to bring this risk down to an acceptable level (Art. 9(5) AIA)."}]},
  {"question": "What are the transparency obligations for providers and deployers of certain AI systems under the EU AI Act, and when do they take effect?", "answer": "Transparency obligations require informing natural persons when interacting with or exposed to AI-generated content, targeting providers and deployers of certain AI systems. These obligations apply from 2 August 2026.", "evidence": [{"page": 19, "quote": "The transparency obligations set out in Article 50 of the AI Act are motivated by the increasing availability of AI-generated content, which can be hard to distinguish from human-generated content. Targeting the providers and deployers of certain AI systems, including generative and interactive AI systems and deepfakes, they aim to ensure that natural persons are informed once they are interacting with AI or exposed to AI generated content, thereby mitigating the risk of misinformation, fraud, or consumer deception [24]. The transparency obligations will apply from 2 August 2026 (Art. 113 AIA)."}]},
  {"question": "In arXiv 2602.11944, what is the definition of a general-purpose AI model (GPAIM) under the EU AI Act?", "answer": "A general-purpose AI model (GPAIM) is defined as an AI model that displays significant generality and is capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks, including those trained with a large amount of data using self-supervision at scale.", "evidence": [{"page": 19, "quote": "A general-purpose AI model (GPAIM) is defined as an AI model \"that displays significant generality and is capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks [...]\" (Art. 3(63) AIA). This includes models \"trained with a large amount of data using self-supervision at scale\" (Art. 3(63) AIA)."}]},
  {"question": "Which dataset in arXiv 2602.11944 is used to predict whether a student will pass, and how is its target variable processed?", "answer": "The 'oulad' dataset is used to predict if a student will pass. The target feature 'final_result' is binarised to 1 if a person passed and 0 if not.", "evidence": [{"page": 22, "quote": "oulad. The features of the oulad dataset are already ordinal or binary. As the target, we used the feature 'final_result', which we binarised to be 1 if a person passed and 0 if not."} ]},
  {"question": "For the ACSEmployment dataset in arXiv 2602.11944, which features were removed during preprocessing and why?", "answer": "The features ESP, ANC, and MIL were dropped because they were either only recorded for a minority, provided little information, or were mostly unused.", "evidence": [{"page": 21, "quote": "ESP       | Employment status parents   | Dropped, because it is only recorded for persons under the age of 18, a minority in the ACSEmployment prediction task.\nANC       | Ancestry recode             | Dropped, because this feature just tells if a person gave informa- tion on their ancestry/ethnic background (not which!).\nMIL       | Military service            | Dropped, because the vast majority of persons recorded in the ACS data never served in military."}]},
  {"question": "In arXiv 2602.11944, which model class uses 'n_hidden_layers', 'size_hidden_layer', and 'activation' as parameter variations?", "answer": "The multilayer perceptron (MLP) model class uses 'n_hidden_layers', 'size_hidden_layer', and 'activation' as parameter variations.", "evidence": [{"page": 23, "quote": "multilayer perceptron (MLP)  | n_hidden_layers ∈ {1, . . . , 26} size_hidden_layer ∈ {1, . . . , 26} activation ∈ {relu, logistic, tanh}"}]}
]}
